Here is an example of how to style a form using CSS. This example assumes that the form is already created with HTML and that the CSS is added to style it.

```css
/* Style the form */
form {
  width: 300px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 5px;
  background-color: #f8f8f8;
}

/* Style the input fields */
input[type=text], input[type=email] {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 12px 20px;
  margin: 8px 0;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 4px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Style the submit button */
input[type=submit] {
  background-color: #4CAF50;
  color: white;
  padding: 14px 20px;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
  width: 100%;
}

/* Style the labels */
label {
  font-size: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
  display: block;
  color: #333;
}

/* Style the select element */
select {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 12px 20px;
  margin: 8px 0;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 4px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

This CSS code styles the form by setting its width, margin, padding, border, and background color. It also styles the input fields, submit button, labels, and select element. You can customize the styles to fit the design of your website.

